course: dictionary
lesson: 13006
title: Outside words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Externally is an adverb. It tells you that something is on the outside, or comes from outside. The adjective is external, as in an external wall. When you meet a word like this, look at the words around it for clues. «The cream is for external use only.» The word only tells you what to do, and external tells you where the cream goes: on your skin, not inside you.
explain: Externally can also mean from outside a group or organisation. «The spelling test was marked externally, by teachers from another school.» The clue is from another school: the people marking did not work at the school where the children learn. So externally here means by people from outside.
explain: A good check is to swap in on the outside or from the outside and see if the sentence still makes sense. «The box was damaged externally, but the toys inside were fine» becomes «The box was damaged on the outside, but the toys inside were fine.» It works, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Externally means on the outside or from the outside.
fact: «For external use only» on a cream means put it on your skin, never swallow it.
fact: In maths, an external angle is an angle outside a shape.
fact: «Externally marked» tests are marked by people from outside the school.
fact: Other phrases to know: externally applied, meaning put on from outside, and external angle.
exercise: «The cream is for external use only.» What does external use mean? | Use it inside the mouth | *Put it on the outside of your body, on your skin | Swallow it with a glass of water | Keep it in the fridge until bedtime
exercise: «The test was marked externally by teachers from another school.» Who marked the test? | The head teacher of this school | *People from outside the school | The pupils in the class | Their parents at home
exercise: Which word means on the outside? | Internally | Secretly | Quietly | *Externally
test: «The box was damaged externally, but the toys inside were fine.» Where was the damage? | *On the outside of the box | Inside the box, among the toys | Under the table | In the toys themselves
test: In geometry, what is an external angle? | A very small angle at the centre | *An angle outside the shape | An angle inside the shape | A right angle in every shape
exam: «Please use this cream externally only.» What does externally mean here? | *On the skin, on the outside of the body | Very carefully and slowly | Once a day, at bedtime | Inside, swallowed with water
